 ```
 
+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+*   **Precision:** The exponential function in the 2D Gaussian evaluation can underflow to zero for distant pixels. Clamping the power term to a minimum value (e.g., -2.0) prevents numerical instability [S20, unofficial].
+*   **Boundaries:** Gaussians near the camera plane can cause division by zero in the Jacobian computation. A small epsilon should be added to the depth $z$ in the Jacobian calculation [G].
+*   **Degenerate Input:** If the SfM point cloud is sparse or noisy, initialization may fail. Random initialization can be used but converges slower [S19, unofficial].
+*   **Covariance Stability:** Directly optimizing the covariance matrix can lead to non-positive semi-definite matrices. Using quaternion and scale parameterization ensures validity [S6][S25, unofficial].
